WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.761 --> 00:00:14.649
That afternoon Nancy ran outside, urgently looking for Tom.

2
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.292
The old man was in the barn cleaning harnesses.

3
00:00:18.312 --> 00:00:23.936
"You'll never guess who's sitting in the parlor," Nancy said breathlessly.

4
00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:28.160
"John Pendleton, and he's come to see Miss Polly!"

5
00:00:30.016 --> 00:00:32.117
Tom looked up from polishing a brass buckle.

6
00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:34.258
"You're joking."

7
00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:37.659
Nancy shook her head.

8
00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:39.900
"I let him in myself.

9
00:00:41.761 --> 00:00:46.203
And I've been meaning to tell you something: he was never Miss Polly's fiancé."

10
00:00:46.223 --> 00:00:48.343
"I know that."

11
00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:52.285
"Well, that story you told me made me think he was.

12
00:00:54.046 --> 00:00:55.786
Anyway, I found out Mr.

13
00:00:55.826 --> 00:01:00.981
Pendleton had been in love with Pollyanna's mother, Jennie, not Miss Polly."

14
00:01:01.001 --> 00:01:03.443
"That's right.

15
00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:07.986
He was the rich, older man Jennie's parents wanted her to marry."

16
00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:13.049
Nancy picked up a piece of straw, twirling it between two fingers.

17
00:01:13.069 --> 00:01:18.352
"I know Miss Polly didn't like Pollyanna's father because he took Jennie far away.

18
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:22.015
But I still don't understand why Miss Polly and Mr.

19
00:01:22.055 --> 00:01:23.656
Pendleton dislike each other."

20
00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:29.460
"That goes back to a few years after Jennie got married."

21
00:01:30.796 --> 00:01:34.197
Tom handed Nancy the clean harness, and she hung it on the barn wall.

22
00:01:34.217 --> 00:01:41.019
"Miss Polly, who was 18 at the time, felt sorry for Mr.

23
00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:46.021
Pendleton. She made an effort to be extra nice to him."

24
00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:47.281
Tom paused.

25
00:01:47.301 --> 00:01:54.623
"Maybe she was too nice because some folks said she was chasing after him."

26
00:01:56.584 --> 00:02:01.521
"Knowing Miss Polly, I'd guess she was embarrassed by all that silly gossip."

27
00:02:03.162 --> 00:02:04.362
"Indeed she was.

28
00:02:05.642 --> 00:02:11.584
And this was around the time she broke off her own engagement, so folks were already talking about

29
00:02:11.624 --> 00:02:13.985
her. Mr.

30
00:02:14.045 --> 00:02:17.025
Pendleton wasn't too keen on the gossip either.

31
00:02:18.446 --> 00:02:24.808
After that, she shut herself up in this house, and he shut himself up in his house on

32
00:02:24.908 --> 00:02:25.888
Pendleton Hill."

33
00:02:27.496 --> 00:02:30.659
Tom started cleaning the leather of another harness with a wet rag.

34
00:02:30.679 --> 00:02:33.661
"So where's Miss Polly now?"

35
00:02:33.681 --> 00:02:38.045
"She was just coming downstairs when I ran out here."

36
00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:45.591
Mr. Pendleton attempted to rise from his chair as Aunt Polly entered the sitting room.

37
00:02:46.731 --> 00:02:48.853
Without shaking his hand, she took a seat.

38
00:02:48.873 --> 00:02:53.077
"I came to inquire about Pollyanna," Mr.

39
00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:53.877
Pendleton said.

40
00:02:53.897 --> 00:02:59.069
"Thank you, she's about the same," Aunt Polly replied sharply.

41
00:02:59.089 --> 00:03:01.750
"But how is she?"

42
00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.251
Mr. Pendleton pleaded for information.

43
00:03:05.471 --> 00:03:08.133
A quick spasm of pain crossed Aunt Polly's face.

44
00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:12.634
"I don't really have much information about her condition."

45
00:03:12.654 --> 00:03:16.636
"But surely the doctor—" "Dr.

46
00:03:16.676 --> 00:03:19.097
Warren himself seems baffled by this case.

47
00:03:20.278 --> 00:03:25.120
He's written to a specialist in New York, and that doctor has agreed to come here to examine

48
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.957
Pollyanna." "Can you tell me anything about her injuries?"

49
00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:37.243
"A slight cut on the head, a few bruises, and damage to the spine that caused paralysis from

50
00:03:37.263 --> 00:03:38.003
the hips down."

51
00:03:41.506 --> 00:03:44.708
Mr. Pendleton moaned and was silent for a few moments.

52
00:03:44.728 --> 00:03:48.870
"How has Pollyanna reacted to being paralyzed?"

53
00:03:50.712 --> 00:03:56.876
"She doesn't seem to really understand, and I hesitate to say more to her until the specialist arrives.

54
00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.086
She's glad her legs are broken like your leg was.

55
00:04:02.087 --> 00:04:05.309
She doesn't want to be a lifelong invalid like Mrs.

56
00:04:05.409 --> 00:04:09.392
Snow." Through a blur of tears, Mr.

57
00:04:09.432 --> 00:04:12.234
Pendleton saw the pain in Aunt Polly's own eyes.

58
00:04:14.235 --> 00:04:17.658
He remembered how Pollyanna had said she couldn't leave Aunt Polly.

59
00:04:19.539 --> 00:04:21.801
And this made him decide to confess something to her.

60
00:04:21.821 --> 00:04:26.324
"I recently tried to get Pollyanna to come live with me," he said.

61
00:04:27.592 --> 00:04:29.553
"I thought I would adopt her and make her my heir."

62
00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.034
At this point Aunt Polly stopped listening.

63
00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:38.395
She thought about what a brilliant future Pollyanna would have with Mr.

64
00:04:38.415 --> 00:04:42.096
Pendleton. He had so much more money than she did.

65
00:04:43.657 --> 00:04:48.878
Then Aunt Polly remembered Pollyanna's saying that she loved being called "dear" by someone who belonged to her.

66
00:04:49.939 --> 00:04:54.660
And Aunt Polly thought about how dreary her own future would be without Pollyanna in the house.

67
00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:58.049
"How did Pollyanna respond to that?"

68
00:04:58.469 --> 00:04:59.669
Aunt Polly said harshly.

69
00:05:00.949 --> 00:05:02.570
"She said she wanted to stay with you."

70
00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.051
Mr. Pendleton pulled himself to his feet.

71
00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:09.372
"And she thought you wanted her to stay."

72
00:05:11.092 --> 00:05:13.853
Without looking at Aunt Polly, he headed for the front door.

73
00:05:15.374 --> 00:05:17.134
But he heard Aunt Polly by his side.

74
00:05:17.154 --> 00:05:22.716
"When the specialist comes and I know something definite, you'll hear from me."

75
00:05:27.016 --> 00:05:29.260
Aunt Polly slipped her trembling hand into Mr.

76
00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.407
Pendleton's. "Good-bye and thank you for coming.

77
00:05:33.928 --> 00:05:35.911
Pollyanna will be pleased to know you were here."
